{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["The sense of <b>\"And Yosef settled them and gave them a holding\"</b> is that he settled them in the choicest part of the land, and in a holding that he gave them, for he did not want them to be like sojourners in the land, but acquired houses for them and gave them the inheritance of field and vineyard. This was with Pharaoh's authorization, for they had said, \"to sojourn in the land we have come,\" not to dwell permanently, and when the famine passes we shall return to our land. But Pharaoh said to Yosef, \"Settle your father,\" meaning that he should settle them as inhabitants of the land dwelling in the land of Goshen."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:01.605213936Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}